menu "hassctrl audio"

    config HC_AUDIO
        bool "Audio output"
        depends on HC_BOARD_HAS_AUDIO
        default y
        help
            Sound through the board's I2S amplifier and speaker (hc::board::Info::audio_*): the
            audio task, the Sound page of Settings and the `sound` console command. Only boards
            with an amplifier offer it; without it none of the audio code is in the firmware.

    config HC_AUDIO_TOUCH_SOUND
        bool "Touch sounds"
        depends on HC_AUDIO
        default y
        help
            A short click for every tap on a button, a tile or a row, switched on and off in
            Settings, Sound. Without it the click and its switch are not in the firmware.

    config HC_AUDIO_MP3
        bool "MP3 files"
        depends on HC_AUDIO
        default y
        help
            Plays MP3 files from the file system (/fs/sounds), such as the alarm sounds, with
            Espressif's esp_audio_codec. Without it only the built-in sounds play.

    config HC_UI_PLAYER
        bool "Audio player"
        depends on HC_AUDIO && HC_SDCARD
        default y
        help
            Plays WAV files (16 bit PCM) and, with HC_AUDIO_MP3, MP3 files from the SD card: a tap
            on one in the file manager of Settings opens the player, with pause, seek and a
            spectrum analyser. Without it the file manager only lists, renames and deletes.

    config HC_AUDIO_ALARM
        bool "Alarm clock"
        depends on HC_AUDIO
        default y
        help
            An alarm in Settings that rings at a time and on chosen days, at full volume, with
            snooze. The sounds are the built-in beeps and, with HC_AUDIO_MP3, the MP3 files.

    config HC_MIC
        bool "Microphone"
        depends on HC_AUDIO && HC_BOARD_HAS_MIC
        default y
        help
            The microphone of the board's audio codec on the same I2S port as the speaker: its
            gain or automatic level control and a level meter in Settings, Sound, console `mic`.
            Without it the codec's input stays off and none of the microphone code is in the
            firmware.

endmenu
